<div class="what-is">
  <h2>What is Daemonless?</h2>
  <p>
    Daemonless is a fleet of <strong>FreeBSD-native OCI images, stacks, and network appliances</strong> that execute directly on the FreeBSD kernel. It pairs the isolation of Jails with standard container workflows across <a href="https://fjord.daemonless.io"><strong>fjord</strong></a>, <strong>Podman</strong>, <strong>AppJail</strong>, <a href="https://sylve.io"><strong>Sylve</strong></a>, <a href="https://freecore.org"><strong>FreeCORE</strong></a>, and any OCI-compliant runtime—with zero Linux virtual machine overhead.
  </p>
</div>

